WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.280
LARRY P. ARNN: Every
time you make a choice,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.510
it places a mark on your soul,
and it makes you what you are.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.985
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.790
So this is a class about ethics.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.140
What is that?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.330
SPEAKER 2: The study
of human character--

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.267
what one ought to do.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.100
LARRY P. ARNN: What do
we mean by character?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.298
SPEAKER 2: The recurrent
habits of action

00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:26.840
that you follow
through in your life.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.650
LARRY P. ARNN: You mean habits?

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.500
SPEAKER 3: It's the
steady state of--

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.680
it's formed through habits,
so you have the steady state

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.680
through which you'll
act in a particular way

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.470
because of the kind
of character you have.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.250
LARRY P. ARNN: I
argue that ethics is

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.300
the study of how best to live.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.916
Why is ethics important?

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.714
SPEAKER 4: Because we're trying
to figure out how to be good.

00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:55.466
LARRY P. ARNN: Good.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:57.073
Good is important.

00:00:57.073 --> 00:00:59.240
Give me another definition
of that word, [? Juan. ?]

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.275
SPEAKER 5: Of ethics?

00:01:00.275 --> 00:01:01.620
LARRY P. ARNN: Yeah.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.075
SPEAKER 5: I would say
development of your character.

00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:07.932
LARRY P. ARNN: Character,
the Greek word [GREEK]..

00:01:07.932 --> 00:01:09.140
SPEAKER 6: Is it like a mark?

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:09.973
LARRY P. ARNN: Yeah.

00:01:09.973 --> 00:01:14.420
Mark, etch, engrave, tattoo.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.470
Not paint on the surface.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.930
Dig in.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.073
Character is dug in,
something deep in us.

00:01:23.073 --> 00:01:24.740
It's what [? Stephen ?]
said down there.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.800
He said, learning
how to be good.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.750
And that is the whole question.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.690
We almost never ask
that question today.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:38.110
We introduce the young to
learning, where in education it

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.360
means lead forth.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.010
We leave off forth.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.380
And that means we introduce
the young to education

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.450
with an invitation
for them to become

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.770
whatever they want to be.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.520
But they could become
ostriches, maybe,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.490
but they wouldn't be
very good at that.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.100
It's the reason ethics
is a big subject.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.740
It is the first subject.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.290
And this is the first book
ever written about it.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.440
And I will tell you, back
in the Paleolithic era,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.590
when I was in graduate
school, in the first class I

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.160
had with a great man, he
called this one of the greatest

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.720
books ever written.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.483
So somebody read
the first sentence.

00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:17.150
Was does it say?

00:02:20.078 --> 00:02:23.270
SPEAKER 7: "Every art and
every inquiry, and likewise

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:27.140
every action and choice,
seems to aim at some good,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.240
and hence it has
been beautifully said

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.800
that the good is that at
which all things aim."

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.380
LARRY P. ARNN: Now look at
the nouns in that sentence.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.838
They're all fundamental words.

00:02:37.838 --> 00:02:38.630
What does art mean?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.540
SPEAKER 2: Technical knowledge.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.040
Yeah.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.028
Yeah, a craft.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:42.820
Something you make.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.020
LARRY P. ARNN: So you
said the word "technical,"

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.090
and the Greek word is [GREEK].

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.070
That's making.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.290
It doesn't mean
in the background

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.380
is Raphael's School of Athens.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.940
That's fine art.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.040
That's high art.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.810
But it has in
common with whoever

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.180
made that glass right
there that it was produced.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.050
It was made.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:07.100
It was designed and
executed according to skill

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.730
and with the purpose in mind.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:11.720
And the first claim
is that every time we

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.950
do that, we aim at some good--

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:16.730
that we're good.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.813
We're going to have to
figure out what that means.

00:03:18.813 --> 00:03:19.770
What's an inquiry?

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.455
SPEAKER 8: Just a question.

00:03:21.455 --> 00:03:24.320
LARRY P. ARNN: It's something
more than a question, isn't it?

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.290
The word is
"methodose" in Greek.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.500
And a method.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.860
In other words, undertake it.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:35.160
It's just, heck, I wonder
what's going to happen tomorrow,

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.840
and then you go on
about your life.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.650
That's not an inquiry.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.560
We're going to find
out what ethics is.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:43.730
This is an inquiry.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.180
And also, remember, we're
going to encounter in book one,

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:52.310
Aristotle saying the reason
this book is to be read

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.720
is to become good.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.570
This is an urgent inquiry.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.760
And this inquiry,
like every other,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.280
he says, aims at some good.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.200
Action, what's that word?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.700
Praxis, you know
what that means?

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.090
SPEAKER 9: Yeah, it's doing.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.210
LARRY P. ARNN: Yeah.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.090
We get practice, practical
from it, practice.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.530
Every time we act.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.660
And then the last is choice.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.760
If you had to pick
one of these words,

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.870
that word is crucial
because choice

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.710
is at the center of the
building of character.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:33.960
In this word "choice" is found
the basis of human freedom.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.200
Because it's not just that
you're free to choose,

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.690
it's also that your
choices matter very much.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:44.160
And the claim is, every
time you make a choice,

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.510
it places a mark on your soul,
and it makes you what you are.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.480
And nobody makes
them all perfect.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:56.220
Anybody who's determined to
make them well, every day,

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.400
and having failed some
that day, start again

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.740
in the morning, those
people become good.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.255
And we'll find out, not
only good, also happy.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.760
I'm Larry Arnn, president
of Hillsdale College.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.130
You will find, if you look
at our online courses,

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.740
that they cover the whole
range of human learning,

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:25.250
all the high and fundamental
things everyone needs to know.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.530
They are free because
we have always

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.500
wished to provide sound
learning to anyone

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.800
who wishes to have it.

